{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.QDeformedCommutator","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.QDeformedCommutator","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Units"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.qDeformedCommutator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.qDeformedCommutator","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-deformed-commutator.lean#L30-L38","doc":"The **q-deformed commutator** `[X̂, P̂]_q := J · ℏ_q` of the fibre\nobservables on `P¹(ℂ)`, with `ℏ_q = 1 - q⁻¹` the quantum Planck constant and\n`J` the complex structure on the Levi distribution (`J² = -Id`).\n\nStated over a generic `[CommRing K]` with `q : Kˣ` a unit (§7c): this is\nexactly the ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]`, where `q⁻¹` is a ring element\nrather than a field inverse. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:q-deformed-commutator","label":"def:q-deformed-commutator","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-deformed-commutator.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}